<article class="env-corollary" id="061J">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/061J">Corollary <span data-tag="061J">9.1.7.4</span>.</a> Let $\lambda $ be an uncountable regular cardinal. Then every filtered $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ can be realized as the colimit of some diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  A \rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}\quad \quad (\alpha \in A) \mapsto \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\alpha }, \]
</div>
<p> where $(A, \leq )$ is a $\lambda $-directed partially ordered set and each $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\alpha }$ is a $\lambda $-small filtered $\infty $-category. Moreover, $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is also a colimit of the diagram $\{  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\alpha } \} _{\alpha \in A}$ in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$. </p>
</article>
